  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the retail price of one pack of glue sticks at the school-supply store? Mr. Jackson’s fourth-grade class has 28 students.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 6; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"I should also tell you: the school-supply store sells each pack of glue sticks for $6.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"The store sells each pack of glue sticks for **$6**. Therefore, the retail price of one pack is:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$6}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Here's another detail: the store does not offer discounts on glue-stick packs.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Since the store charges **$6 per pack** and does not offer discounts, the retail price of one pack is:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$6}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many packs of glue sticks does Mr. Jackson need to buy so every student can have 2 glue sticks? By the way, here are some relevant details: Mr. Jackson wants to give each student 2 glue sticks. Mr. Jackson can only buy whole packs and expects to have some extra glue sticks left over.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mr. Jackson needs:\n\n\\[\n28 \\times 2 = 56\n\\]\n\nglue sticks in total. However, the number of glue sticks in each pack is not given. If each pack contains \\(n\\) glue sticks, he must buy\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left\\lceil \\frac{56}{n} \\right\\rceil \\text{ packs}}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(\\lceil\\ \\rceil\\) means rounding up to the next whole pack.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
