  "task_assistant_messages": [
    "1. The problem tells us only that Mr. Jackson’s class has 28 students.\n2. It gives no information about the number of glue sticks, total cost, or price per pack.\n3. Therefore, the retail price cannot be determined from the given information.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price cannot be determined.}}\n\\]",
    "Knowing that the class has 27 students still does not provide the price of one pack of glue sticks. We would need additional information, such as the total cost or the number of packs purchased.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price cannot be determined.}}\n\\]",
    "With 27 students and 9 glue sticks per pack:\n\n\\[\n27 \\div 9 = 3 \\text{ packs}\n\\]\n\nHowever, the problem still does not state the cost of a pack or the total cost. Therefore, the retail price of one pack cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price cannot be determined from the given information.}}\n\\]",
    "With 27 students and 8 glue sticks per pack:\n\n\\[\n27 \\div 8 = 3\\text{ remainder }3\n\\]\n\nSo the class would need **4 packs** to give each student a glue stick. However, no price information is provided, so the retail price of one pack cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The retail price cannot be determined from the given information.}}\n\\]",
    "The store sells each pack of glue sticks for **$6**. Therefore, the retail price of one pack is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6}\n\\]",
    "Since the store charges **$6 per pack** and does not offer discounts, the retail price of one pack is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6}\n\\]",
    "Mr. Jackson needs:\n\n\\[\n28 \\times 2 = 56\n\\]\n\nglue sticks in total. However, the number of glue sticks in each pack is not given. If each pack contains \\(n\\) glue sticks, he must buy\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left\\lceil \\frac{56}{n} \\right\\rceil \\text{ packs}}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(\\lceil\\ \\rceil\\) means rounding up to the next whole pack."
  ],
